From 51fd6faec2289033525c7a40a5307caade5bdfe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:22:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] script: proximity snapping, scroll-snap-stop and re-snapping
 after layout

Snap containers with `scroll-snap-type: proximity` now snap like Chromium:
only when the chosen snap position is within a third of the scrollport size
of where the scroll would otherwise end. Directional scrolls (keyboard,
wheel, and now scrollBy(), which Chromium also treats as directional) no
longer pass over a snap area with `scroll-snap-stop: always`; Home and End
go to the end of the box without stopping, as in Chromium.

Each snap remembers the snap targets it chose, and every rendering update
re-snaps snap containers that are not being scrolled to those targets, so a
carousel stays on the same slide when it is resized or content is inserted
before the slide. When a target goes away the box snaps anew from its
current position.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
